From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QEAFIVELS Kernel Bring-up <kernel@qeafivels.local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] initramfs: unpack supplied ramdisk when skip_initramfs is set

The Violet bootloader appends skip_initramfs to the command line even when
fastboot boot supplies a non-empty external ramdisk. In the current 4.14
initramfs.c, do_skip_initramfs causes populate_rootfs() to call
default_rootfs() and free initrd_start without unpacking it. The kernel then
mounts the Android root partition and executes its /init.

Keep the skip behavior for normal boots with no supplied initrd, but allow a
valid external initramfs to be unpacked when the bootloader supplied one.
This is needed for QEAF's RAM-boot diagnostic image. It does not change the
boot partition or the persistent device tree.

This patch is based on the official MiCode Violet source snapshot
(violet-q-oss, base 4.14.117). It is NOT yet verified against the exact
4.14.215-azure-Pixel+ source tree and must not be shipped until rebuilt and
tested with the matching source/toolchain.

---
 init/initramfs.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/initramfs.c b/init/initramfs.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/init/initramfs.c
+++ b/init/initramfs.c
@@ -623,9 +623,7 @@ static int __init populate_rootfs(void)
 {
 	char *err;
 
-	if (do_skip_initramfs) {
-		if (initrd_start)
-			free_initrd();
+	if (do_skip_initramfs && !initrd_start) {
 		return default_rootfs();
 	}
 
